    <section>

      <h2>1. Master Windows Snap Layouts</h2>

      <p>Windows 11 introduced <strong>Snap Layouts</strong> to organize multiple apps side-by-side with ease. Hover your mouse over the maximize button of any window and choose your preferred layout. This feature helps you multitask like a pro — open your browser, file explorer, and notes side by side without clutter.</p><div class="highlight">Pro Tip: Press <strong>Win + Z</strong> to instantly open the Snap Layout grid!</div>

</section>

<section>

  <h2>2. Enable God Mode for Advanced Control</h2>

  <p>Windows has a hidden “<strong>God Mode</strong>” folder that gives you access to nearly all system settings in one place. Here’s how to enable it:</p>

  <ul>

    <li>Right-click your desktop → New → Folder.</li>

    <li>Rename it to <code>GodMode.{ED7BA470-8E54-465E-825C-99712043E01C}</code>.</li>

    <li>Open it to reveal 200+ hidden settings in one dashboard!</li>

  </ul>

  <div class="highlight">Caution: Don’t delete the God Mode folder while open—it can cause temporary UI glitches.</div>

</section>

<section>

  <h2>3. Use Virtual Desktops Like a Pro</h2>

  <p>Virtual desktops allow you to separate work, gaming, and study spaces. To use them:</p>

  <ul>

    <li>Press <strong>Win + Tab</strong> → click “New Desktop.”</li>

    <li>Switch between them with <strong>Ctrl + Win + Left/Right Arrow</strong>.</li>

  </ul>

  <p>You can rename desktops for clarity — for example, “Work,” “Play,” or “Projects.”</p>

</section>

<section>

  <h2>4. Clipboard History & Cloud Sync</h2>

  <p>Copy multiple items and reuse them anytime! Activate Clipboard History by pressing <strong>Win + V</strong>. It stores your recent copied text and images.</p>

  <div class="highlight">Enable sync between devices by toggling “Sync across your devices” in Clipboard Settings → System → Clipboard.</div>

</section>

<section>

  <h2>5. Storage Sense & Disk Cleanup Automation</h2>

  <p>Keep your system fast and clutter-free using <strong>Storage Sense</strong>. Go to Settings → System → Storage → enable Storage Sense. It automatically deletes junk files, old downloads, and temporary updates.</p>

  <p>For deeper cleanup, run <strong>Disk Cleanup</strong> (search it in Start) and remove unused system files.</p>

</section>

<section>

  <h2>6. Dynamic Wallpapers and Themes</h2>

  <p>Make your PC come alive with motion wallpapers and vibrant color themes. Apps like <strong>Wallpaper Engine</strong> or <strong>Lively Wallpaper</strong> let you set live, interactive wallpapers that sync with your music or system performance.</p>

  <p>To change theme colors: Settings → Personalization → Colors → Choose your accent color.</p>

</section>

<section>

  <h2>7. Optimize Startup Apps</h2>

  <p>Speed up boot time by disabling unnecessary startup apps. Go to Task Manager → Startup tab → right-click and disable unwanted programs.</p>

  <div class="highlight">Pro Tip: Keep antivirus and drivers enabled, but disable tools you rarely use.</div>

</section>

<section>

  <h2>8. Use PowerToys for Advanced Control</h2>

  <p>Microsoft PowerToys is an open-source toolkit that unlocks pro-level features like FancyZones (custom window layouts), PowerRename, and Keyboard Manager.</p>

  <p>Download from Microsoft Store or GitHub and customize your workflow instantly.</p>

</section>

<section>

  <h2>9. Secure Your PC with Windows Defender & BitLocker</h2>

  <p>Windows Defender now offers cloud-based threat protection that’s fast and automatic. Pair it with BitLocker encryption to protect your files if your device is lost or stolen.</p>

  <ul>

    <li>Go to Settings → Privacy & Security → Device Security.</li>

    <li>Enable BitLocker (Windows Pro versions).</li>

  </ul>

  <div class="highlight">Bonus: Turn on “Tamper Protection” in Defender for extra safety.</div>

</section>

<section>

  <h2>10. Automate Tasks with Windows Copilot & Power Automate</h2>

  <p>Windows 11 introduces <strong>Copilot</strong>, an AI assistant that helps with summaries, settings changes, and productivity tasks. Combine it with <strong>Power Automate</strong> to automate file organization, reminders, and reports.</p>

  <p>This duo turns your PC into a smart assistant capable of handling routine work while you focus on creativity.</p>

</section>

<section>

  <h2>Bonus Trick: Hidden Commands in Command Prompt & PowerShell</h2>

  <p>Try commands like:</p>

  <ul>

    <li><code>ipconfig /flushdns</code> – Clear DNS cache and fix connection errors.</li>

    <li><code>sfc /scannow</code> – Scan and repair corrupted files.</li>

    <li><code>chkdsk /f</code> – Check and fix disk errors.</li>

  </ul>

  <p>These commands can instantly fix issues that would otherwise need third-party apps.</p>

</section>

<section>

  <h2>Final Thoughts</h2>

  <p>Windows 10 and 11 are packed with powerful hidden tools that many users never explore. By mastering these tricks, you’ll boost performance, security, and creativity — all without extra software. Try one or two each week, and soon your PC will feel brand new.</p>

  <p>If you found this article helpful, share it with friends or follow me for more weekly <strong>Tech Tricks</strong> and guides!</p>

</section>

